.TH OKFSMITH 1 "September 2026" "okfsmith 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
okfsmith \- forge messy documents into OKF v0.2 knowledge bundles
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B okfsmith
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.I COMMAND
.RI [ ARGS ]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B okfsmith
is a Python CLI that ingests messy documents (PDFs, markdown, wiki dumps,
Notion exports) and emits spec-conformant OKF v0.2 knowledge bundles:
markdown files with YAML frontmatter, plus reserved
.B index.md
and
.B log.md
files. Every concept carries provenance
.RI ( sources[] ),
a trust tier, and lifecycle metadata, and every bundle is checked by a
built-in \(sc11 validator. The bundle is always the first positional
argument.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B init \fIBUNDLE\fR [\-\-force] [\-\-yes]
Scaffold
.B index.md
and
.B log.md
in
.IR BUNDLE .
Refuses a non-empty directory unless
.B \-\-force
is given (asks for confirmation unless
.BR \-\-yes ).
.TP
.B ingest \fIBUNDLE\fR \fISOURCE\fR... [\-\-recursive] [\-\-no\-llm] [\-\-model \fINAME\fR] [\-\-dry\-run] [\-\-quiet]
Parse, section, and extract each
.I SOURCE
(file or directory) into draft concepts. Sources are SHA-256 fingerprinted:
already-ingested files are skipped.
.B \-\-no\-llm
writes one draft concept per section, fully offline.
.TP
.B validate \fIBUNDLE\fR [\-\-format text|json] [\-\-strict]
Check OKF \(sc11 conformance. Exit 0 means conformant.
.B \-\-strict
also fails on warnings.
.TP
.B list \fIBUNDLE\fR [\-\-format text|json] [\-\-tier \fITIER\fR]
List concepts, optionally filtered by trust tier
.RI ( unverified ,
.IR machine-confirmed ,
.IR human-reviewed ).
.TP
.B read \fIBUNDLE\fR \fICONCEPT_ID\fR [\-\-format text|json]
Print one concept (id is the bundle-relative path without
.BR .md ).
.TP
.B graph \fIBUNDLE\fR [\-\-format text|json|mermaid|html] [\-\-output \fIFILE\fR]
Show concept links. The
.B html
format writes a self-contained offline viewer
.RI ( viz.html ).
.TP
.B mcp \fIBUNDLE\fR [\-\-transport stdio|sse|streamable\-http]
Serve the bundle to AI agents over MCP. Requires the
.B mcp
extra.
.TP
.B doctor
Check dependencies, optional extras, Ollama reachability, and temp-dir
writability.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success (for
.BR validate :
conformant).
.TP
.B 1
Expected failure; the message starts with
.BR "error [CODE]:" ,
e.g.
.BR "error [bundle-not-found]:" ,
and includes a hint. No tracebacks.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error (bad flags, invalid enum choices, conflicting options).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B OKFSMITH_MODEL
Default model name for LLM extraction.
.TP
.B OPENAI_API_KEY
API key for OpenAI-compatible backends (never read from files).
.TP
.B OKFSMITH_BASE_URL
Base URL for OpenAI-compatible backends.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I completions/okfsmith.bash
.TQ
.I completions/okfsmith.zsh
.TQ
.I completions/okfsmith.fish
Shell completion scripts (source from your shell rc file, or run
.BR "okfsmith --install-completion" ).
